tags: service-file, on_filesystem

A source of a dependency: a file in the filesystem of the service that declares the
dependency. The file holds the bytes of the Service of the dependency: the bytes whose
hash is the hash of the dependency.

The value is the path of the file: the segments separated by "/", with no "/" at the
start, as UTF-8. Example: deps/worker.service.

A node that does not know this source ignores it. A party that reads the file checks
its hash before it uses it. The source does not change the service that the hashes
name.

=== formal
class=source
content=the serialized Service of the dependency; its hash is the hash of the dependency
